    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0953" n="927" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg927"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 242: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the United States Delegation</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d603-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-25T18:51:00-04:00">May 25, 1954—6:51
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tedul 123. Limit distribution. Hope your talk
                    with Eden resulted in British agreement go
                    along on Thai initiative in SC,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d603-f2"/> since we are eager begin proceedings without delay.</p>
                <pb facs="0954" n="928" xml:id="pg928"/>
                <p>We would expect Khoman would be able to
                    send Thai letter raising this matter in SC before
                    end of week, and that SC meetings could be
                    scheduled, say, for Wednesday, Thursday and Friday next week (June 2, 3 and 4).
                    If SC action could be completed that quickly, and
                    assuming Soviet veto, we would expect General Assembly might meet on or shortly
                    after June 15th.</p>
                <p>Would appreciate it if you could ask Eden
                    to request Dixon in New York to
                    cooperate to extent possible in arranging for SC
                    proceedings.</p>
                <p>We will want to approach Indians as soon as we know Eden has consented.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d603-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d603-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Popper of UNA/UNP. Repeated
                    to USUN as telegram 588.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d603-f2" n="2" xml:id="d603-f2-content">
                <p>Regarding the Thai decision to make an appeal to the United Nations, see the
                    memorandum of conversation, <ref target="#pg919">p. 919</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
